# Subjects and education types

- **Do not show preset subject codes** (`efl`, `ffl`, etc.) in the UI. The subject field uses full localized labels via `subjectLabelLocalized` / datalist options built from `REPORT_SUBJECTS` + tenant custom names.
- **Form text → storage**: use `resolveDefaultSubjectInputToStorage` from `@/lib/subjectFormResolve` so typed labels map to ISO codes when they match a preset in any UI language; otherwise the trimmed string is stored as a custom subject (length rules in `@/lib/subjects`).
- **Storage → input display**: use `subjectFieldDisplayValueFromStored(raw, uiLang)` so codes become labels; legacy unset `efl` shows empty so the placeholder (“Define subject name”) appears.
- **Education type** is `grade_rubric_profile` / `GradeRubricProfile` from `GRADE_RUBRIC_PROFILES` in `@/lib/gradeRubricProfile`. Iterate that array for UI sections and options—when a new profile is added, subject lists and labels extend with it. Use `gradeRubricProfileDisplayLabel(t, rp)` for consistent labels.
- **Tenant school type is the source of truth for the whole rubric**: when the owner changes `tenants.default_grade_rubric_profile` (settings PATCH), the API runs `syncTenantClassesGradeRubricProfile` so **every** `classes.grade_rubric_profile` matches and any `classes.cefr_level` that is invalid for the new profile is cleared. Class level options, grade metric labels, report inputs, and AI prompts must all resolve from that effective class rubric (`parseGradeRubricProfile(klass.grade_rubric_profile, …)`), not from the tenant default alone.
- **POST `/api/tenants/[tenantId]/classes`**: new rows always use `tenants.default_grade_rubric_profile` for `classes.grade_rubric_profile` (ignore client `grade_rubric_profile` so stale UI cannot create a primary tenant with a language class).
- **GET `/api/tenants/[tenantId]/classes/[classId]`** calls `alignClassGradeRubricWithTenantIfNeeded`: if the class row’s `grade_rubric_profile` differs from `tenants.default_grade_rubric_profile`, the row is updated (invalid `cefr_level` cleared). Self-heals legacy rows and drift; requires migration **0032** so `classes.grade_rubric_profile` exists (insert throws with a clear error if the column is missing).
- **Subject suggestions** are built per `GradeRubricProfile` in `@/lib/subjectOptionsByEducationType.ts` (`subjectSuggestionLabelsForRubric`). **ClassWorkspace** reads the class row’s `grade_rubric_profile` (kept in sync with the tenant default as above). The class card shows **only** that profile’s suggestions (single datalist) and **only** that profile’s custom subjects in the manage dropdown (no other programme’s content).
- **Secondary metric row titles (UI + AI English)** live only in `@/lib/i18n/secondaryRubricMetricI18n.ts` (`SECONDARY_METRIC_EN_BY_KEY`, `secondaryMetricUiLabel`, `secondaryMetricEnglishForAi`). Do **not** reuse `REPORT_METRIC_I18N` (language school) or `PRIMARY_METRIC_EN` for secondary. Add non-English copy via `SECONDARY_METRIC_UI_OVERRIDES` in that file—never merge secondary strings into primary/language tables.
- **AI report drafts** (`reportCommentPrompts.ts`, `shortCourseReportCommentPrompt.ts`): `ReportDraftPromptContext.gradeRubricProfile` must match the dataset rubric. CEFR-only homework restrictions apply **only** when `gradeRubricProfile === "language"`. Primary vs secondary **grading context** (one class teacher vs multiple subject strands) is injected via `schoolGradingContextRulesForRubric`.
- **Report subject override** (`ReportEditor`): render preset language `<option>`s only when `parseGradeRubricProfile(klass.grade_rubric_profile, "language") === "language"`; strip `inputs.subject_code` on load when the class is not language acquisition.
- **Custom subject rows** in tenant JSON include `name` and `rubric_profile`. Custom names are **scoped per education type**; the API persists them that way. Built-in languages are not stored as custom rows.
- **Changing education type** away from language should clear the subject field when it resolved to a **preset language code** (user-facing label), so primary/secondary classes do not keep a language-only preset.
